"entity": {
"name": "Ingredion Incorporated",
"description": "Ingredion, Inc. engages in the development, production, and sale of food and beverage ingredients, primarily starches and sweeteners. The firm is involved in transforming corn, tapioca, potatoes, plant-based stevia, grains, fruits, gums, and vegetables into value-added ingredients and biomaterials for the food, beverage, brewing, and other industries. It operates through the following geographical segments: Texture & Healthful Solutions (T&HS), Food & Industrial Ingredients-Latin America (F&II-LATAM), Food & Industrial Ingredients-U.S./Canada (F&II-U.S./Canada), and All Other. The T&HS segment offers its solutions to the global market. The company was founded in 1906 and is headquartered in Westchester, IL.",
"rbics_econ": "Non-Energy Materials",
"rbics_sector": "Chemical, Plastic and Rubber Materials",
"rbics_subsector": "Specialty and Performance Chemicals",
